      'Whether a Chikankari or handicraft-export path is genuinely the stronger route for your situation',
      'What your income trajectory looks like on the current path over the next few years',
      'Which expensive wrong turn is most urgent to stop repeating right now',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Skill direction tied to Lucknow's actual economy",
    listItems: [
      'A structured, realistic state-exam preparation and backup plan if that path fits your situation',
      'Design, production, quality-control, or export-business skills if the handicraft economy fits your situation better',
      'Government-administration career planning if a secretariat or direct-recruitment role is part of the picture',
      'A clearer route toward earlier financial freedom from your actual starting point',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'A lower-friction way to start moving',
    listItems: [
      'Online guidance accessible across India with no local-access dependence',
      'A realistic career target and the clearest path to reach it from where you are now',
      'One concrete next step instead of a theory discussion you still have to decode yourself',
    ],
  },
];

const onlineAdvantageItems = [
  {
    title: 'You can start from home, hostel, coaching PG, or workshop',
    body: 'Career counselling is available online in Lucknow and across India. That means the decision does not have to wait for a nearby office or one local slot opening up. The useful filter is whether the guidance improves the next move enough to matter.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Online guidance can sit alongside family and mentor conversations, not compete with them',
    body: 'When a multi-attempt exam plan or a Chikankari family-business tie is part of the picture, the harder conversations often need to include family or mentors. Online sessions make it easier to include that context and join from wherever you already are.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The stronger comparison is not nearby versus far away - it is generic versus genuinely useful',
    body: "A nearby or well-known coaching institute can still leave you with generic advice that ignores Lucknow's specific state-exam or handicraft-export context. The better filter is whether the guidance gives you stronger skill direction, proof-of-work thinking, and a more practical next step.",
  },
];

const objectionItems = [
  {
    title: 'Should I keep attempting UPPSC or a state-government exam, or move to a different path?',
    body: "That depends on your realistic timeline, attempt history, and backup options - a structured attempt-and-backup plan is a genuinely strong approach. An open-ended coaching cycle with no exit plan is a weaker bet than it looks.",
  },
  {
    title: 'My family runs a Chikankari or handicraft-export business - is that still a good reason to choose this path?',
    body: 'A family business can be a genuine advantage for entry and trust, but the career choice itself should still rest on your own aptitude, interest, and an honest look at the growth ceiling, not on the business already existing.',
  },
  {
    title: 'I am worried about wasting more time before choosing a direction',
    body: 'That is usually the best reason to act now. In a city where a state-exam coaching cycle and a handicraft-export path can each look equally serious, getting clear before another attempt-year passes is exactly when counselling has the highest return.',
  },
];

const prepItems = [
  {
    title: 'The real decision you need to solve first',
    body: 'Bring the actual question creating pressure right now, whether that is an exam-attempt decision, a handicraft-business direction, or income growth.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The serious options you are already considering',
    body: 'Write down the two to four routes you are actually comparing. Stronger counselling happens when the real trade-offs are visible from the start.',
  },
  {
    title: 'What feels risky, delayed, or expensive',
    body: 'Be clear about what you do not want to repeat: another unplanned attempt year, a family-pressure default, or more time wasted in confusion.',
